error[E0277]: `Contains` is not a leaf operator, so it cannot be applied at a path
 --> tests/ui/op_at_path_not_a_leaf.rs:9:25
  |
9 |     operator(op::AtPath(op::Contains));
  |     --------            ^^^^^^^^^^^^ `op::AtPath` takes a leaf operator
  |     |
  |     required by a bound introduced by this call
  |
  = help: the trait `Leaf` is not implemented for `Contains`
  = note: `op::AtPath` applies `op::Eq`, `Lt`, `Lte`, `Gt`, `Gte`, `Between` or `Matches` at a path; `op::Contains` and `op::ContainedBy` compare whole documents, and an accessor does not nest
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Leaf`:
            stack_encrypt::op::Between
            stack_encrypt::op::Eq
            stack_encrypt::op::Gt
            stack_encrypt::op::Gte
            stack_encrypt::op::Lt
            stack_encrypt::op::Lte
            stack_encrypt::op::Matches<C>
  = note: required for `AtPath<Contains>` to implement `Operator`
note: required by a bound in `operator`
 --> tests/ui/op_at_path_not_a_leaf.rs:6:17
  |
6 | fn operator<Op: op::Operator>(_: Op) {}
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `operator`

